# VSS neon for 5-60 K: species-ID diameter(m) omega tref(K) alpha.
# Fitted (least squares in ln eta, uniform in ln T over 5-60 K, T_ref = 23 K) to
# the dilute-gas viscosity from full quantum Chapman-Enskog collision integrals
# on the ab initio Ne-Ne potential of Hellmann, Bich & Vogel, Mol. Phys. 106,
# 133 (2008); the calculation reproduces Bich et al. (2008) / CRC eta to 0.1%
# at 100-300 K. eta(23 K) = 3.61 uPa s. Fit error: <= 6% over 5-60 K.
# alpha from the computed Schmidt number (Sc = 0.75 at 5-60 K).
# Bird's 273 K VHS set (d 2.766e-10, omega 0.66) extrapolated to 23 K
# over-predicts eta by 61% (89% at 10 K): its cross section is ~1.9x too small.
# Calculation: ~/orcd/scratch/ne_collision_integrals/ (pot.py, qs.py, fit*.py).

Ne  4.59e-10  0.883  23.0  1.43
